dispatched item shows "enviando" without cancel. | Must | AC-006 |
98-| FR-006 | Attempt fencing: each dispatch is an attempt of the item's `clientMessageId`. Every create and fence 
request carries the item's attempt generation (monotonic per key). The server accepts a create only if its generation 
is the current one for that (sender, conversation, key) at the moment of commit, and a fence with generation g 
atomically either returns the stored message (item resolves as delivered) or makes every generation below g unable to 
commit — including requests still in the network that have not reached the server; a fence or create with a generation 
older than the server's current one is rejected. When an attempt ends without a usable response (network error, 
timeout, tab closed, lease expired, superseded, HTTP 5xx), the item is unknown; before any cancel, expiry, takeover, 
