109-| FR-017 | The typing indicator stays visible while the other person types continuously and disappears at most 5 s 
after they stop, blur the composer, send, leave the conversation, or close the tab. | Must | AC-017 |
110-| FR-018 | The indicator names typists: 1 → "Ana está digitando…", 2 → "Ana e Bruno estão digitando…", 3+ → "N 
pessoas estão digitando…", in direct, group, and room conversations. | Must | AC-018 |
111-| FR-019 | Typing signals travel only on a private Realtime topic whose join and send are authorized for current 
conversation members; anon clients, authenticated non-members, and public-topic attempts never receive them; the app 
detects the user's own removal from a conversation through a signal that does not depend on still having access to 
that conversation and leaves the topic within 5 s. Payload: user identity and typing flag only. Residual risk accepted 
(D3, D6): a tampered client of a removed member may receive and send typing signals until its access token expires. | 
Must | AC-019 |
112-| FR-020 | A user never sees their own typing indicator, including from their other tabs or devices. | Must | 
AC-020 |
113-| FR-021 | While connectivity and Realtime are healthy, within 5 s and without reload, focus change, or reconnect: 
when the user reads messages (fully or partly) on one tab/device, their other tabs/devices show the same unread counts 
and read state, and the sender's receipt summary/details agree with the stored receipts on all of the sender's 
sessions. During an outage, FR-016 deadlines apply. | Must | AC-021 |
114-| FR-022 | While connectivity and Realtime are healthy, a message the user sends from one device/tab appears on 
their other devices/tabs within 5 s without reload; during an outage, FR-016 deadlines apply. | Must | AC-022 |
115:| FR-023 | In the composer, typing "@" opens a list of the conversation's current members except the user, 
filtered as they type, operable by mouse and keyboard (arrows, Enter/Tab, Esc); choosing inserts a highlighted 
mention. In a room the list contains only members of the room conversation. Typed "@name" text that was not chosen 
from the list is plain text. | Must | AC-023, AC-024 |
116:| FR-024 | On first creation the server stores mentions in the same transaction as the message, as application 
user IDs of conversation members at that time other than the sender; other requested IDs create no mention. The 
original submitted composition (content, reply target, requested mention IDs) is what replays are compared against: an 
unchanged replay returns the stored message without re-validating recipients; a different composition under the same 
key returns `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`. Clients cannot write mention records directly; only conversation members can 
read them. | Must | AC-024, AC-046 |
117-| FR-025 | With the Phase 4 desktop-notification toggle on and permission granted, a mentioned user receives one 
desktop notification for a message that mentions them (direct, group, room, thread reply), titled "<Autor> mencionou 
você em <conversa>" with the full text; clicking opens the conversation. Before emitting, the app confirms with 
authoritative data, under the current identity, that the user is still a member and (for rooms) mentioned; then, with 
no further awaits before display, it re-checks that the same user is still signed in and that no removal signal for 
that conversation has arrived; otherwise the pending notification is discarded, as it is on any account switch or 
sign-out. Residual race accepted (D6): a removal that the app has not yet received when the final check runs may let 
that one notification show. Suppression is browser-wide: no tab notifies if any of the user's tabs in that browser is 
visible and viewing that conversation, regardless of which tab receives the event first. | Must | AC-025, AC-026, 
AC-049 |
118-| FR-026 | Mentions render distinctly for everyone; a message that mentions the viewing user is highlighted for 
that user with a non-color cue. | Must | AC-027 |
119-| FR-027 | The client records metric events — send latency (press → server confirmed), outbox wait time, send 
outcomes by reason, Realtime stream drops/recoveries and outage duration, polling activations and duration — in a 
bounded buffer (oldest dropped when full) and sends them fire-and-forget in batches of at most 50 events and 16 KB, at 
most one delivery in flight, each aborted after 5 s, dropping batches under overload. The authenticated, per-user 
rate-limited route rejects oversized requests, accepts only closed event/reason enums and bounded numeric fields, 
drops anything else, adds a server-derived app version, and writes structured log lines under BR-013. | Must | AC-028 |
120-| FR-028 | Metrics never block, slow, or break messaging: messaging code never awaits metric delivery; an 
erroring, hanging, or overloaded metrics route changes no messaging behavior or timing and shows no error. | Must | 
AC-029 |
121-| FR-029 | `mark_conversation_read` refuses to mark a conversation for a user who is not a member of it. | Must | 
AC-030 |
122-| FR-030 | `get_unread_counts` is not executable by the `anon` role; authenticated use keeps working. | Must | 
AC-031 |
