162-
163-### Integrations
164-- Supabase Postgres, Realtime (`postgres_changes`, private broadcast topics), Auth (server routes use 
`createSupabaseServerClient` + `auth.getUser()`).
165-- Browser APIs: IndexedDB, Web Locks and/or BroadcastChannel for cross-tab claims and signals, Notification API 
(Phase 4), Page Visibility.
166-- Hosting/Supabase logs as the metrics sink; no new external analytics dependency.
167-
168:## 10. Constraints and assumptions
169-
170-### Constraints
171-- Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, routes, and 
query keys rather than parallel implementations.
172-- Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages link 
to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
173-- Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated E2E); Firefox desktop (verified). Safari and mobile not required.
174-- No service worker; background notifications are page-level only.
--
192-| Hung holder when connectivity returns | Its attempt is superseded at once; D1 deadline holds (AC-041). |
193-| Two tabs come online together | One drain claim per conversation; only the oldest unresolved item is eligible; 
no overlapping create requests for that conversation; each stored and shown once, in order (AC-005). |
194-| Owning tab closes or hangs mid-request | Closed or lease expired: another tab fences and finishes once; while 
the lease is live no other tab dispatches (AC-041). |
195-| Cancel races a claim | Exactly one wins; a cancelled item is never dispatched; a dispatched item cannot be 
cancelled (AC-006). |
196-| Lost access before reconnect | First item fails definitively with text; later items of that conversation wait; 
other conversations deliver (AC-007). |
197-| Access regained after failure | "Tentar de novo" delivers it, then the waiting items in order (AC-008). |
198:| Other definitive outcomes (404, 400, 413, 422) and 5xx | Definitive → failed with text; 5xx → unknown → fence 
(AC-046). |
199-| `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` | Failed; "Tentar de novo" resends the content under a new key, once (AC-043). |
200-| Server rate limit during drain; concurrent same-key requests | Items stay pending, retried automatically; quota 
charged once per stored message; replays/fences use a separate budget (AC-009). |
201-| Laptop asleep > 24 h | Not-stored items become "expirada"; stored ones resolve as delivered (AC-010, AC-042). |
202-| Offline attachment / voice | Upload failure: per-file error + retry; create failure after upload: Phase 4 
composer failure; nothing in the outbox (AC-011). |
203-| IndexedDB unavailable or write fails | Nothing dispatched; text stays in the composer with the storage message 
(D5) (AC-039). |
204-| Identical texts sent twice; Realtime arrives before the HTTP response | One bubble per message, matched by key 
(AC-050). |
--
209-| Realtime drop < 5 s | No "Reconectando…" banner (AC-014). |
210-| Only the conversation-list stream fails | Banner after 5 s and polling after 30 s follow its health; recovered 
independently (AC-015, AC-016). |
211-| Stale poll returns after a newer Realtime update | Newer/enriched state kept; no duplicates (AC-048). |
212-| Realtime down > 30 s, tab hidden | No polling; on visible, fetch immediately then every 15 s (AC-016). |
213-| Typist closes the tab or leaves the conversation mid-typing | Indicator disappears ≤ 5 s (AC-017). |
214-| Anon, outsider, public-topic, or removed-member typing access | Refused / no events; removed member's app leaves 
at once; tampered client bounded by D3 (AC-019). |
215:| Forged mention IDs, plain "@name", changed mentions on replay, recipient removed before replay | No mention for 
non-members/self/plain text; changed composition → 409; unchanged replay returns the stored message (AC-024, AC-046). |
216-| Recipient removed or account switched after commit but before the notification is shown | No notification once 
the app has the removal/switch signal; a removal not yet received at the final check is the accepted D6 race (AC-049). 
|
217-| Manual retry of an expired item hits 429 or an unknown outcome | New 24 h window: retried/fenced automatically 
(AC-010). |
218-| Partial reads by others during a Realtime-only outage | Receipt summaries and open reader details update via 
polling (AC-016). |
219-| Hidden tab receives a mention event first while another tab views that conversation | No notification (AC-026). |
220-| Malicious, oversized, hanging, or sustained metrics traffic | Rejected or dropped; route rate-limited; messaging 
unaffected (AC-028, AC-029). |
221-| Restored conversation no longer accessible | Conversation list opens without error (AC-032). |
--
260-- AC-017 (FR-017; must-not R1-q16 E): Given B types continuously for 15 s, then A sees the typing indicator at 
every 1 s sample; when B stops, it disappears within 5 s; when B closes the tab mid-typing, within 5 s; when B 
switches to another conversation mid-typing, within 5 s.
261-- AC-018 (FR-018): Given a group or room with A, B, C, D, when B types, A sees "<B> está digitando…"; B and C → 
"<B> e <C> estão digitando…"; B, C, D → "3 pessoas estão digitando…"; a direct conversation shows the single-typist 
phrase.
262-- AC-019 (FR-019, BR-009): With real local Realtime: an anon client, an authenticated non-member, and a client on 
the public topic name receive no typing events of conversation X and cannot send typing events members receive; member 
A receives B's typing; when member E is removed from X while subscribed (and while X is not open in E's drawer), E's 
app leaves the topic within 5 s and shows no further typing for X (integration + E2E).
263-- AC-020 (FR-020, BR-009): Given A has two tabs and a second device on X, when A types in tab 1, then neither tab 
2 nor the second device shows A as typing.
264-- AC-021 (FR-021): Given healthy connectivity and A on two devices with 6 unread in X, when A reads only the first 
3 on device 1, then within 5 s device 2 shows 3 unread for X; after reading the rest, 0. Given A is the sender of 
messages read by B, then A's receipt summary/details on both of A's sessions match the stored receipts within 5 s.
265-- AC-022 (FR-022): Given healthy connectivity and A on two devices, when A sends on device 1, then it appears once 
on device 2 within 5 s without reload.
266:- AC-023 (FR-023, BR-010): Given A types "@" in a room conversation, then the list shows only room-conversation 
members other than A, filters as A types, and supports arrows/Enter/Tab/Esc and mouse; choosing "Bruno" inserts a 
highlighted mention; a workspace user who never joined the room chat is not listed.
267:- AC-024 (FR-023, FR-024, BR-010; must-not R1-q16 F): On the real route and local DB: a message mentioning a 
non-member ID and the sender's own ID stores no mention for either and notifies neither; a replay that changes only 
the requested mention IDs returns `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED` and changes nothing; a message whose text contains 
"@Bruno" typed without selection stores no mention; a forced failure of mention storage stores neither the message nor 
any mention; anon and non-members cannot read mention records; no client can insert/update/delete them directly.
268-- AC-025 (FR-025, BR-011): Given B has notifications enabled and permission granted, B's tab hidden or viewing 
another conversation, when A mentions B in a room, then B receives exactly one notification "<A> mencionou você em 
<sala>" with the full text; clicking opens that room in the drawer; a room message without a mention of B produces 
none.
269-- AC-026 (FR-025, BR-011; must-not R1-q16 C): Given B has notifications enabled, then a DM mention yields exactly 
one notification; a thread-reply mention yields one; with B's two tabs where the hidden tab receives the event first 
and the visible tab is viewing that conversation, none; A's own message yields none for A; with the toggle off, none; 
a mention across B's two hidden tabs yields exactly one.
270-- AC-027 (FR-026): Given A's message mentions B, then all members see the mention styled distinctly, and only B 
sees the whole message highlighted with a non-color cue.
271-- AC-028 (FR-027, BR-013): Given a send, a stream recovery, and a polling episode occur, then the metrics route 
writes structured lines with enum event type/reason, durations, and server-derived version; a scan finds no message 
text, names, emails, or user/conversation IDs; a payload with unknown fields, free-text strings, out-of-range numbers, 
or a forged version produces no such values in the logs; a request over 50 events or 16 KB is rejected; requests 
beyond the per-user rate limit are rejected; an unauthenticated request is rejected and produces no metric log line.
272-- AC-029 (FR-028): Given the metrics route errors, and separately hangs, and separately is flooded with sustained 
traffic, when A sends, goes offline, and reconnects, then AC-001/AC-002 behavior and timing hold, at most one metrics 
request is in flight from A's tab, a hanging metrics request is aborted after 5 s, the client buffer never exceeds its 
bound (oldest events dropped), and no error is shown.
273-- AC-030 (FR-029): Given user E is not a member of X, when `mark_conversation_read` is invoked for E and X through 
every role that can execute it, then the call is refused and E's read state for X is unchanged (integration, local DB).
274-- AC-031 (FR-030): Given the `anon` role, when it calls `get_unread_counts`, then permission is denied; an 
authenticated member still gets correct counts (integration, local DB).
275-- AC-032 (FR-031, BR-016): Given the drawer open on X, when A reloads, then it reopens on X; given A lost access 
to X, then the list opens with no error; given C signs in on that browser, then C does not get A's conversation; given 
the drawer was closed, it stays closed.
276-- AC-033 (FR-032): The existing Phase 4 messaging E2E regression suite and DB integration suite pass after each 
slice; `npm run type-check`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build` pass.
277-- AC-034 (BR-014, §10): Every migration of the phase is applied locally with recorded rollback SQL; before any 
online application, the currently hosted build (git ref confirmed by the owner) and the Phase 4 build each pass a 
send/read/unread smoke against the migrated local database (legacy unkeyed writes still work); at phase end, after 
explicit owner authorization, it is applied to `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko`, the catalog is read back from that target, and 
a runtime smoke check passes; the hand-off states the app is ready to deploy after the migrations.
278:- AC-035 (§12): The Supabase/RLS review gate passes for every migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API 
route change.
279-- AC-036 (BR-015): Each new E2E spec passed 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and in Edge; the key flows (outbox, 
banner, typing, mentions) were verified in Firefox and recorded; no unit test was added; every touched unit test was 
replaced and deleted, recorded in TRACK.
280-- AC-037 (FR-014, §13): The banner is announced via a polite live region, item states have text labels, and the 
sign-out dialog and mention list are fully keyboard-operable.
281-- AC-038 (FR-002, FR-006, BR-004): Given A's create request is stored but its response is dropped, then the item 
becomes unknown, the fence resolves it as delivered without a second create, and B sees it once.
282-- AC-039 (FR-033, R1-q2 A, D5): Given IndexedDB is unavailable (and separately a failing outbox write), when A 
sends a text message, then zero create requests are sent, the text and reply target stay in the composer, and "Este 
navegador não permite guardar mensagens; libere o armazenamento do site" is shown.
283-- AC-040 (FR-001): Given A is online and the create request is held, when A closes the tab before the server 
confirms, then on reopening the app the item is fenced and B sees the message exactly once.
284-- AC-041 (FR-004): Given tab 1 holds the claim and its create request is held, then tab 2 sends no create request 
for that conversation while tab 1's lease is live; when tab 1 is closed (and separately when its lease expires while 
it hangs), tab 2 fences and the message is stored once. Given tab 1's attempt hangs across an outage, when 
connectivity returns with that single item pending and quota available, then it is delivered within 10 s (D1) and 
stored once.
285-- AC-042 (FR-006, FR-009): Given an unknown item whose request was actually stored, when A tries to cancel it or 
its 24 h passes, then no cancel is offered before fencing, the fence resolves it as delivered, and it never shows 
"expirada".
286-- AC-043 (FR-007): Given an item rejected with `CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED`, when A clicks "Tentar de novo", then 
its content is stored once under a new key and the conflicting stored message is unchanged.
287-- AC-044 (FR-011, BR-001, §12): Given A's drain is paused before dispatch and the browser's session switches to C 
(a member of the same conversation), when the drain would resume, then no create or fence request is sent as C; a 
crafted create or fence request carrying A as expected sender with C's session is rejected and stores or fences 
nothing; an anon fence/lookup is rejected; C fencing or looking up a key that belongs to A's message (with C as 
sender) neither returns A's message nor affects A's attempts.
288-- AC-045 (FR-006, BR-004): With real local Postgres and the real routes: (a) attempt 1's INSERT is blocked (row 
lock held by the test) while a fence for that key reports not stored; on release attempt 1 does not commit; (b) 
attempt 1's request is held before reaching the server while a fence runs; when released it is rejected as stale; (c) 
a stale fence (older generation) arriving after a newer attempt was dispatched is rejected and the newer attempt 
commits; in every case at most one message is stored (integration + E2E).
289:- AC-046 (FR-007, FR-024, BR-005): On the real route: 403 (missing conversation or not a participant), 400 
(invalid reply target), and 413 (content too large) are classified definitive in the drawer (failed with text); a 5xx 
returned after the request reached the server is classified unknown and fenced; an unchanged replay after a mentioned 
recipient left the conversation returns the stored message (not 409) and notifies no removed recipient.
290-- AC-047 (FR-011, FR-013): Given a real create response and a real fence response held while the browser switches 
from A to C, and separately while A confirms Sair mesmo, and separately (same identity) while the item is cancelled or 
superseded by a newer generation, when the responses are released, then no A content appears in C's view, no deleted 
or cancelled item reappears, and no newer claim or attempt is changed.
291-- AC-048 (FR-016): Given a poll response is held while Realtime delivers a newer state (a reaction, a receipt, an 
attachment message, a mention) and older history pages are loaded, when the stale poll is released, then the feed 
keeps the newer state, the loaded pages, and one bubble per message.
292-- AC-049 (FR-025, BR-011; must-not R1-q16 F): Given B is mentioned and B's authoritative check has already 
returned "member" but display is held, when B's app receives B's removal signal (and separately when the browser 
switches to another account) before display, then no notification is shown; given the check is held before it runs and 
B is removed, then no notification is shown.
293-- AC-050 (FR-034): Given A sends two messages with identical text (one plain, one replying to a message) and 
Realtime delivers each before its HTTP response, then each shows as exactly one bubble in both of A's tabs throughout, 
matched by `clientMessageId`.
294-
295-## 15. Test strategy
296-
297-- Test levels:
298:  - Integration (local Supabase Postgres/Realtime and real API routes): sender and attempt-generation fencing 
incl. stale requests and stale fences (AC-044, AC-045), insertion quota, request budget, and fence budget (AC-009), 
fence/lookup authorization incl. anon and other users' keys (AC-038, AC-042, AC-044), outcome classes (AC-046), 
mention atomicity/validation/replay/RLS (AC-024, AC-046), private typing-topic authorization incl. 
anon/outsider/public topic (AC-019), `mark_conversation_read` membership (AC-030), `get_unread_counts` anon revoke 
(AC-031), metrics route auth, enums, sizes, rate limit, redaction (AC-028).
299:  - E2E (Playwright, real UI; two or more real accounts; two tabs of one account; a second device as a separate 
browser context): every other AC. Network shaping only — the app, routes, and Supabase stay real: browser-context 
offline mode; blocking only the Realtime WebSocket or a single stream; holding a request or response by delayed 
pass-through to the real server; dropping a response or replacing it with a gateway 5xx after pass-through; disabling 
IndexedDB or failing its writes in the page (AC-039). Old-build compatibility: the hosted and Phase 4 builds are run 
locally against the migrated database (AC-034). Expiry may use a test-controlled clock without changing the product 
rule.
300-  - Unit: none (BR-015).
301-- Tests trace to acceptance criteria by AC ID; written from the ACs before or with the implementation.
302-- Test data: accounts A, B, C, D, E in one company; a DM, a group, and a room conversation; a room the test can 
remove A/E from and re-add; a way to exhaust A's create quota locally.
303-- Environments: local Supabase for integration/E2E; Chrome and Edge for automated E2E; Firefox verification of key 
