168: ## 10. Constraints and assumptions
169: 
170: ### Constraints
171: - Next.js App Router, TypeScript strict, Supabase, TanStack Query; reuse existing hooks, repositories, routes, 
and query keys rather than parallel implementations.
172: - Identity: RLS compares `users.supabase_uid` with `auth.uid()::text`; foreign keys use `users.id`; messages link 
to rooms through `conversations.room_id`.
173: - Browsers: Chrome and Edge desktop (automated E2E); Firefox desktop (verified). Safari and mobile not required.
174: - No service worker; background notifications are page-level only.
175: - No message text, names, or identifiers in metrics (BR-013); no external analytics service.
176: - The sign-out confirmation must not change the Presence logout sequence (presence-safety rules apply to that 
touch point).
177: - Online database changes only at phase end with explicit authorization (BR-014); the hosted app currently runs 
the pre-Phase-4 build until the owner deploys, so new server contracts must stay compatible with that build and with 
the Phase 4 build until deployment: unkeyed legacy message writes and existing RPC/route signatures keep working 
against the migrated database.
178: - Repository test policy (BR-015); type-check, lint, and build must pass.
179: - Timing parameters chosen under the owner's delegation (D4) and adjustable in planning only with owner approval: 
claim request timeout 30 s, lease 45 s, metrics batch â‰¤ 50 events / 16 KB, one metrics delivery in flight, 5 s 
metrics abort.
180: 
181: ### Assumptions
182: - None beyond the user-confirmed answers and owner decisions recorded in `state.md`.
