752: comment on function public.create_message_attempt(uuid, uuid, text, text, uuid, uuid, bigint, jsonb, uuid[], 
integer, integer) is
753:   'Phase 5 T2/T3/T4: creates a text message (keyed or not), or a message with 1-5 pending uploads of its sender 
(Phase 4 T12/T15 rules), committing only when the attempt generation is current for (sender, conversation, key) at 
commit time (a generation-less keyed create only when no fence state exists). In the same transaction it stores the 
mentions requested in p_composition->''mentionIds'' (at most 50 UUIDs; only current members other than the sender; 
MENTION_IDS_INVALID otherwise) and, for a winning insertion, charges the sender''s ''message:create'' insertion quota 
(p_insert_quota_limit per p_insert_quota_window_seconds; both NULL = no charge): RATE_LIMITED (quota exhausted) or 
RATE_LIMIT_UNAVAILABLE (charge failed) roll it back. Returns {message_id, created, composition, message, 
mentioned_user_ids}; message and mentioned_user_ids describe the created row (created=true only); created=false is a 
replay (never charged, no mention written). Raises NOT_PARTICIPANT (42501) for a non-member sender, ATTEMPT_SUPERSEDED 
when fenced and MESSAGE_DELETED when a generation-carrying create would recreate a deleted message. Service role only; 
callers authorize the sender and validate the attachment policy first.';
