2: -- (spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience): server-validated atomic
3: -- @mentions and the current-member roster.
4: --
5: -- Mentions (FR-024, BR-010):
6: --   * public.message_mentions (message_id, mentioned_user_id = users.id) holds
7: --     the application users a message mentions. Rows are written ONLY by
8: --     public.create_message_attempt, inside the transaction of the message's
9: --     first creation (every message insert of this build runs there since T3:
10: --     keyed text, unkeyed text, attachments/voice, and the Phase 4 wrapper),
11: --     right after the INSERT and the attachment links and before the
12: --     commit-time fence check and the insertion-quota charge: if the mention
13: --     insert fails, or the attempt is fenced or over quota afterwards, the
14: --     whole create rolls back (no message, no attachment link, no mention, no
15: --     quota charge).
16: --   * The requested ids travel in the stored ORIGINAL composition
17: --     (p_composition -> 'mentionIds', route-normalized: lowercase, distinct,
18: --     sorted, at most 50 UUIDs). A mention row is created only for ids that are
19: --     conversation_members of the conversation at that moment and are not the
20: --     sender; every other requested id (non-member, outsider, unknown, the
21: --     sender) creates nothing but stays in the stored composition, so a replay
22: --     is compared against what was requested (the route answers 409
23: --     CLIENT_MESSAGE_ID_REUSED when the requested mention set differs, and 200
24: --     with the stored message for an unchanged replay â€” membership is not
25: --     re-validated on replay, so a recipient removed since does not turn an
26: --     unchanged replay into a refusal, and no mention is added or removed).
27: --     Replays and lost same-key races never write mentions.
28: --   * Absent vs empty (decision recorded for T4): a composition without a
29: --     'mentionIds' key (every composition stored before this migration, and
30: --     every request without mentions) means "no mention requested", exactly
31: --     like an empty array. Phase 4 replays of pre-T4 keyed messages therefore
32: --     still answer 200; a replay that now requests mentions for such a message
33: --     answers 409. Without a composition (keyed messages created before T2, or
34: --     by a raw insert) a replay matches only when it requests no mention.
35: --   * Mentions require a client key (the route refuses mentionIds without
36: --     clientMessageId), so unkeyed creates (hosted pre-Phase-4 client) and the
37: --     Phase 4 wrapper (null composition) never write mentions.
38: --   * create_message_attempt keeps its T3 signature; its result gains
39: --     'mentioned_user_ids' (sorted ids actually stored) on a winning
40: --     insertion. public.create_message_with_attachments (Phase 4 signature)
41: --     now builds its {message_id, created} result explicitly, so no new key of
42: --     the inner result ever reaches a Phase 4 server (same output as before).
43: --   * Read: RLS SELECT for authenticated conversation members only (same rule
44: --     as message_attachments / message_reactions: the mention's message is in
45: --     a conversation the caller belongs to). anon holds no privilege;
46: --     authenticated holds SELECT only, and there is no INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE
47: --     policy, so no client can write, change or delete a mention. service_role
48: --     holds SELECT and INSERT (for the SECURITY INVOKER create function).
49: --     Deleting a message or a user cascades to its mentions (referential
50: --     actions run as the table owner). The table is NOT added to the Realtime
51: --     publication (Realtime payloads unchanged).
52: --
53: -- Roster (FR-023): public.list_conversation_members(conversation_id) returns
54: -- (user_id, display_name, avatar_url) for every CURRENT member of the
55: -- conversation (public.conversation_members, so a removed member is excluded)
56: -- to a caller that is itself a current member; anyone else (non-member,
57: -- missing conversation, no app user) gets NOT_PARTICIPANT (42501). SECURITY
58: -- DEFINER (conversation_members RLS is own-row only), search_path '', caller
59: -- resolved with private.current_app_user_id() (users.supabase_uid =
60: -- auth.uid()::text). EXECUTE: authenticated only.
61: --
62: -- Security: every function is search_path '' with schema-qualified
63: -- references; EXECUTE revoked from public, anon and authenticated (Supabase
64: -- default privileges grant it on new functions) and granted explicitly
65: -- (create_message_attempt / wrapper: service_role; roster: authenticated).
66: -- Table privileges on public.message_mentions are revoked from every API role
